{"id":"leetcode-443","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"String Compression","summary":"Given an array of characters, compress it by appending each character or character followed by its count for consecutive groups.","statement":"Given an array of characters, compress it by appending each character or character followed by its count for consecutive groups. Store the compressed string in the input array, handling lengths of 10 or more by splitting them. Return the new length of the array, using no extra space.","constraints":["1 <= chars.length <= 2,000; each item is one letter, digit, or symbol.","Compress consecutive runs in the original array: write the character, then decimal count digits only for counts greater than one.","Return the meaningful prefix length k. Only chars[:k] is graded; the tail is ignored. Target constant extra space."],"topics":["strings","two-pointers"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"compress_characters","parameters":[{"name":"chars","annotation":"list[str]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"int","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"returned_prefix","mutated_parameter":0,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def compress_characters(chars: list[str]) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def compress_characters(chars):\n    read = write = 0\n    while read<len(chars):\n        end = read+1\n        while end<len(chars) and chars[end]==chars[read]:\n            end += 1\n        count = end-read\n        chars[write] = chars[read]\n        write += 1\n        if count>1:\n            first_digit = write\n            while count:\n                chars[write] = chr(48+count%10)\n                write += 1\n                count //= 10\n            left,right = first_digit,write-1\n            while left<right:\n                chars[left],chars[right] = chars[right],chars[left]\n                left,right = left+1,right-1\n        read = end\n    return write\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def compress_characters(chars):\n    from itertools import groupby\n    result=[]\n    for char,group in groupby(chars):\n        count=len(list(group))\n        result.append(char)\n        if count>1: result.extend(str(count))\n    return len(result)\n","def compress_characters(chars):\n    read = write = 0\n    while read<len(chars):\n        end = read+1\n        while end<len(chars) and chars[end]==chars[read]:\n            end += 1\n        count = end-read\n        chars[write] = chars[read]\n        write += 1\n        if count>1:\n            count %= 10\n            first_digit = write\n            while count:\n                chars[write] = chr(48+count%10)\n                write += 1\n                count //= 10\n            left,right = first_digit,write-1\n            while left<right:\n                chars[left],chars[right] = chars[right],chars[left]\n                left,right = left+1,right-1\n        read = end\n    return write\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":1},"hints":["Read one complete run before overwriting its compressed output.","Use a read pointer for runs and a write pointer for the meaningful output prefix.","Write the run character. For count>1 write its digits, then advance to the next unread run; return write.","Compression never expands a run, so writes cannot overtake unread input. Extract count digits arithmetically and reverse that digit segment in place for O(1) auxiliary space."],"editorial":"Save the end of each run before writing. A singleton emits only its character; longer runs emit the character followed by count digits. The reference writes count digits least-significant first, then reverses just that output segment without allocating a count string. Since each compressed run is no longer than its input run, unread data is safe. The judge checks both the integer length and the actual modified prefix, not the unused tail.","tests":[{"id":"lc-443-1","arguments":[["a","a","b","b","c","c","c"]],"expected":{"return":6,"prefix":["a","2","b","2","c","3"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Return 6 and write [a,2,b,2,c,3] into the first six cells. Returning a separate string is not sufficient.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-2","arguments":[["a","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b"]],"expected":{"return":4,"prefix":["a","b","1","2"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Return 4 with prefix [a,b,1,2]. A singleton has no count, and 12 occupies two character cells.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-3","arguments":[["a"]],"expected":{"return":1,"prefix":["a"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-4","arguments":[["a","a"]],"expected":{"return":2,"prefix":["a","2"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-5","arguments":[["a","b","c"]],"expected":{"return":3,"prefix":["a","b","c"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-6","arguments":[["a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a"]],"expected":{"return":3,"prefix":["a","1","0"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-7","arguments":[["a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a","a"]],"expected":{"return":3,"prefix":["a","1","1"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-8","arguments":[["a","a","b"]],"expected":{"return":3,"prefix":["a","2","b"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-443-9","arguments":[["a","b","b"]],"expected":{"return":3,"prefix":["a","b","2"]},"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanatio